      "created_at": "2013-04-07T09:56:07.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Another quick clarification question…</p>\n<p>When the heirloom flips and is in play in front of a hero does it become a hero target? My instinct is yes (and this is the way my wife and I played it) but a clarification on this is very important since there are so many \"non-hero\" and \"non-villian\" damaging effects in the game. Our logic is that if the hero's gain benefits from the card it is a hero target and if Kismet gains benefits then it is a villian target. But again, we want to ensure that every victory we have is ligitimate–after all, real heros never cheat!&nbsp; <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\"></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:56.429Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
